{
  "name": "SensitiveFail",
  "comment": "Fails an assertion where %MyIdentity% (which carries a [Sensitive] PrivateKey)\nis the Actual value. Drives Identity into both AssertionError.Actual and the\ncaptured Variables snapshot — the outer test verifies test.report masks the\nPrivateKey as '******' before writing. %MyIdentity% is a reserved DynamicData\nthat lazily get-or-creates the default identity, so the fixture is idempotent\nacross runs (no \"already exists\" error).",
